+## When `beforeSession` throws
+
+- `beforeSession` sits inside the `try` block, so a throw there reaches the same `catch` and `finally` as any other failure in the turn: the caller still sees the rejection unchanged, `onError` receives the thrown error with the same argument shape as any other orchestrator failure, and `afterSession` fires on the way out ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+- On that path a hook may assume the turn never started: the provider was never called, so no tool ran and no hook after `beforeSession` in the fire order fired either, while the session still reaches the store's `save` from the same `finally` — an `afterSession` releasing what `beforeSession` allocated can therefore release unconditionally, with no flag of its own to tell "never allocated" from "allocated and finished" ([validated by: saves once and still rethrows when beforeSession fails](../../src/orchestration/sessionSave.test.ts#L93)).
